evacuated from his home mr panayotis  watches his burning village on the news  he's lived there since the day he was  born and in his lifetime he's seen 97  summers  this is his hottest  the smoke completely surrounded us and  we couldn't breathe he says then they  brought us here  this former retirement home reopened as  an evacuation center on friday  last night alone 45 people streamed  through its doors  when we arrived there were a few rooms  available by the time we left they were  gone  many of those now needing this refuge  are distressed still in shock this woman  came to tell us it was british  firefighters who saved her house  i saw you and i said bless you she said  you came here to help greece but still a  huge catastrophe has happened here in  our village 28 houses burned counted one  by one almost all the olive groves  burned sheep burned goats burned  it's not just an international effort  here volunteers from as far away as  athens are staffing this evacuation  center others are sending supplies  with messages of support written on top  of food parcels the words courage and  hope  we need firefighters on the ground and  in the air as we are a difficult region  to get to but local businesses from all  the surrounding areas have instantly  come together to support us  21 villages were evacuated overnight in  this area of the peloponnese but around  lunchtime the conditions get too  dangerous and the roads are closed so  getting out is a race against the clock  people here at least now are safe and  for anyone who's lost their home the  greek government is offering 150 000  euros in compensation but for some  that's not enough and they've chosen to  stay in their evacuated villages  thinking they can somehow do something  to protect their property if they're  there in person and for many they're all  too aware this is a crisis greece could  be facing year after year  a grandfather brought here by worried  relatives is one of the last to secure a  room but he's among thousands in greece  displaced and distressed about what the  future holds sally lockwood sky news in  the peloponnese
 

